well-- the enchantment/benefit behavior, you can just figure out from
playing-- the fact that you can safely enchant them cames from a
quick read of the source (best spoiler of all) after noticing
that +5 would only put you up to 23 str and wondering if I would
blow them up going for 25-- read.c says:

  special_armor = is_elven_armor(otmp) ||
                  (Role_if(PM_WIZARD) && otmp->otyp == CORNUTHAUM) ||
		  (Role_if(PM_VALKYRIE) && otmp->otyp == GAUNTLETS_OF_POWER);
		  
  .....

  s = sobj->cursed ? -otmp->spe : otmp->spe;
                
  if (s > (special_armor ? 5 : 3) && rn2(s)) {
       /* blow up the armor */
  }

so you can see that if your roll is "valkyrie" and the object you are
enchanting has type "gauntlets of power", its considered special--
s is then the enchantment of the armor (or negative if you are reading
a cursed scroll since you will be subtracting)- then if s is greater than (5
if the armor is special, 3 if not) there is a (s-1) in s chance of it
blowing up.

